# OpsCockpit systemd service template (REFERENCE ONLY)

This file is a future deployment reference. It is NOT applied in this phase,
and OpsCockpit development never touches a production host.

## What it would look like

```ini
# /etc/systemd/system/opscockpit.service
[Unit]
Description=OpsCockpit runtime dashboard
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
# Hardened
NoNewPrivileges=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
ReadOnlyPaths=/etc
# The binary reads /proc, /sys, cgroup v2, and runs `ss`/`systemctl show` —
# those are the minimum capabilities it needs. It never talks to a network
# socket of its own beyond the dashboard listener.
User=root
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/opscockpit serve \
  -state /var/lib/opscockpit/state.json \
  -services /etc/opscockpit/services.yaml \
  -listen 127.0.0.1:8090
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

A companion timer would run `opscockpit collect` every N seconds/minutes to
refresh `state.json`.

## Purpose of this directory

Reference templates only. Actual production setup (user creation, directory
layout, unix socket, Nginx/UFW/Docker integration) is a separate phase and is
performed deliberately, never from this repository's CI.
